#: tips.cpp:3
msgid ""
"<p>\n"
"...that you can create shortcuts for your favorite bluetooth device\n"
"and for often dialed numbers? <i>Save as..</i> will create a shortcut\n"
"that optionally includes a phone number. You can put it on the desktop\n"
"or drag it to the Quick Launcher menu.\n"
"</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:13
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can save the conversations as ogg vorbis files with your voice\n"
"on the right channel and the other party on the left?</p>\n"
"<p>See the <i>Configure</i>-menu\n"
"for more options.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:21
msgid ""
"<p>...that recorded conversations contain the called number as ogg tag? </p>\n"
"<p>You can display this information directly with konqueror by selection\n"
"the <i>Info List View</i> view mode.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:28
msgid ""
"<p>...that KBTHandsfree can use data from KAddressbook to complete phone "
"numbers?</p>\n"
"<p>Simply enter the beginning of an existing name or a number.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:34
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can use your phone's voice dialing feature with KBTHandsfree?</p>"
"\n"
"<p>Voice dialing will be activated if you press dial without entering a "
"number.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:40
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can dial numbers directly from kaddressbook under KDE 3.2?</p>\n"
"<p>Just put 'kbthandsfree --dial --phonenumber %N' under\n"
"Settings->Configuration->General->Script-Hooks->Phone</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cpp:47
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can use kbthandsfree as a simple call monitor with several "
"phones?</p>\n"
"<p>The Sony/Ericsson T68i for instance will connect automatically to your "
"computer\n"
"upon incoming calls, if your computer was recognized as a headset, it is the "
"first\n"
"headset in the list of paired devices and you told the phone to use the "
"headset\n"
"when available. Nokia phones don't seem to be able to connect automatically "
"though.\n"
"</p>\n"
msgstr ""
